    "summary": "A Medicaid managed long-term care program for adults 18+ who are a frail elder or have a disability and need ongoing help with daily activities. An MCO coordinates all the person's long-term care services under one benefit.",
    "benefit": "Managed long-term care: help with daily tasks at home, personal care, home modifications, day services, residential care, and more, coordinated by a managed care organization.",
    "howToApply": {
      "url": "https://www.dhs.wisconsin.gov/familycare/index.htm",
      "phone": "800-362-3002",
      "steps": [
        "Contact your local ADRC to find out if you are eligible.",
        "Complete the Long-Term Care Functional Screen and the Medicaid application.",
        "If eligible, choose a managed care organization (MCO) and enroll."
